fix(compose): preserve iOS Safari user-gesture for Photo/Video → compose flow

iOS Safari blocks programmatic file-input .click() that doesn't happen
inside the originating user-gesture handler. The previous wire of
SharedPostCreator's Photo/Video tap was:

  onClick:
    if (context==='social-media') router.push('/compose'); return;
    setPreparingStage('picker');
    fileRef.current?.click();   // never reached on social-media

  AlbumPicker (mounted on /compose):
    useEffect(() => {
      setTimeout(() => fileInputRef.current?.click(), 50);   // BLOCKED by iOS
    }, []);

Result on iPhone: tap Photo/Video → land on the compose picker page →
file input never opens → user has to tap "Open library" manually.
That's exactly the regression Dan described as the original complaint.

Fix: keep the click() inside the user-gesture handler (it works as it
always did). Move the route hop to AFTER the file change event arrives.
In handleFiles, when context==='social-media' AND we got files back,
hand them to composeStore (addMedia + setStep('edit') + reset()) and
THEN router.push('/hub/social-media/compose'). AlbumPicker's auto-fire
becomes irrelevant — by the time /compose renders, the store already
holds media and step='edit' so the user lands directly on EditPostScreen.

Modified files:
  src/components/social/SharedPostCreator.jsx
    • Reverted the early router.push redirect; click(file input) is
      now always in the user-gesture
    • Added composeStore import
    • In handleFiles top-fork: build {id,type,file,url,...} entries,
      reset+addMedia+setStep('edit'), router.push to /compose, return.
      Try/catch fallback drops back to inline staging if anything in
      the handoff throws.

Direct-URL-to-/compose flow still works (no media in store →
AlbumPicker shows the prominent "Open library" empty-state CTA which
opens the picker on user tap — also a real user gesture).

4-pass verification after fix:
  Pass 1 (wiring) — clean. SharedPostCreator now imports useComposeStore;
    handleFiles fork sits before existing inline-staging logic;
    AlbumPicker auto-fire still gated on `media.length === 0` so it's
    a no-op when the store is pre-populated. esbuild parse passes.
  Pass 2 (real-time) — clean. No new Supabase calls; the bgUpload start
    + fn_create_social_post path on /compose is unchanged.
  Pass 3 (adversarial) — clean. The fork is gated on context check
    (only the public social-media composer hits it); club-page and
    other inline contexts unaffected.
  Pass 4 (edge cases) — clean. Empty file selection in handleFiles
    short-circuits before the fork (line 355). Fork wraps in try/catch
    that falls through to inline staging on failure. Fileref value
    cleared so the same files can be re-picked.
